================================================================================
BUG #27 -- bridge1 slave board (pynq_z2_03) PS-eth unreachable
================================================================================

Symptom (2026-05-21 15:00+):
  - The slave PYNQ-Z2 board's PS-side ethernet (192.168.6.101) is unreachable.
  - ARP entry "incomplete"; ping returns "Destination Host Unreachable".
  - The master board (192.168.4.101, z2_02) remains fully alive and reachable.
  - The fpgahub bridge1 lease was acquired and released cleanly -- this is NOT
    a lease or harness issue.

Impact on this release flow:
  - The planned live 20-iter re-test produced 20 rows of 0/16 because every
    deploy targeted the unreachable slave. This is noise, not data.
  - The release bundle itself is fully assembled, checksummed, and verifiable;
    only the live re-run row of this file is meaningless until the slave is
    power cycled.

Required to recover:
  - Physical power cycle of pynq_z2_03 (lab access). Until then any deploy
    against 192.168.6.101 returns 0/16 because the slave SSH probe times out
    on the first call -- not because the bitstream regressed.

This is a TRANSIENT LAB HW FAILURE, not a v1 RC1 release-quality issue.

